\title{SPRING: Semi-Parametric Rank-based approach for INference in Graphical model (SPRING)}
\description{
Provides methods for sparse microbial association network estimation from microbiome count data. The core function implements SPRING (Semi-Parametric Rank-based approach for INference in Graphical models), which estimates latent correlations via a truncated Gaussian copula model and fits sparse graphical models using Meinshausen-Bühlmann neighborhood selection with StARS stability selection. Both quantitative microbiome data and compositional (relative abundance) data are supported; the latter via a modified central log-ratio (mclr) transformation that accounts for zero-inflated counts. The package also provides a synthetic count data generator based on the empirical cumulative distribution function of real microbiome data, enabling reproducible simulation studies under user-specified network structures.
}
